# 2. Single Number II (Two Unique Numbers)

### Steps

1. XOR all elements.
2. Find the rightmost set bit.
3. Divide elements into two groups based on that bit.
4. XOR elements of each group.

```java
class Solution {
    public int[] singleNum(int[] arr) {

        int xorAll = 0;

        for(int ele : arr) {
            xorAll ^= ele;
        }

        int setBit = xorAll & -xorAll;

        int num1 = 0;
        int num2 = 0;

        for(int num : arr) {

            if((num & setBit) != 0) {
                num1 ^= num;
            }
            else {
                num2 ^= num;
            }
        }

        if(num1 < num2) {
            return new int[]{num1, num2};
        }

        return new int[]{num2, num1};
    }
}
```

